# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 111-116 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 13 — CHAPTER 15, 2026-09-22; RUN B1, THE FIRST HALF): the release and its calendar
# (111), the manner of the release, the two years and the loans (112), the foreigner, the pledge and the prozbul (113), the needy and the blessing (114), the
# hearing that grows (115), the receipt's referent, the lending, the ranks of the poor, the hand opened and the measure of need (116) — EVERY ROW READ WHOLE
# in both files (the whole-row rule); every quotation of the shelf CUT by consonants (ch15_ink.SP_ — a miss lands in FAIL, asserted empty by the ledger
# writer); a middah named only where the row argues by one (logic/MIDDOT.md, the code checked before it is typed: I1 the a fortiori, I2 the analogy, I3 the
# paradigm, I8 and I13 named by shape without a code). Speed ruling (c): CONTEXT rows terse. Chapter 14's form (ch14_rows_sifrei_96_103.py).
from ch15_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(111, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AT THE END OF SEVEN YEARS" (15:1) — MIGHT IT BE FROM THE YEAR\'S BEGINNING OR AT ITS END? "END" IS SAID HERE AND "END" IS SAID THERE (31:10): AS THE END SAID THERE IS AT ITS END AND NOT ITS BEGINNING, SO THE END SAID HERE. The head row of piska 111 ({SP_(111, 1, "נאמר", "כאן", "קץ", "ונאמר", "להלן")} "end is said here and end is said there"; {SP_(111, 1, "בסופה", "ולא", "בתחלתה")} "at its end and not at its beginning"): I2 (checked) ON THE WORD "END" — 15:1 and 31:10\'s assembly the Torah\'s two "at the end of seven years" (asserted; Jeremiah 34:14 the Bible\'s third): THE RELEASE FALLS AT THE SEVENTH YEAR\'S END — the compile\'s date; 109:3 reads the same word at 14:28 from the other side (the outside row); the English\'s brackets ask it of field-work, the Hebrew of the release itself. Fresh.')
srow(111, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL MAKE A RELEASE … RELEASE" (15:1-2) — WHENEVER YOU HAVE A RELEASE [OF THE LAND], YOU RELEASE [THE LOAN]. ({SP_(111, 2, "כל", "זמן", "שיש", "לך", "שמטה")} "whenever you have a release"): THE TWO RELEASES BOUND TOGETHER — the land\'s (Exodus 23:11; Leviticus 25:2-7, the kin\'s ledger) and the debt\'s, the second conditioned on the first: the exam\'s question when the land\'s release lapses (Gittin 36a-b; Mishnah Sheviit 10). Fresh.')
srow(111, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"SEVEN YEARS" — MIGHT IT BE SEVEN YEARS FOR EACH ONE [FROM HIS OWN LOAN]? YOU REASON: SEVEN YEARS ARE LAID ON THE RELEASE [OF THE LAND] AND SEVEN YEARS ON THE LOAN — AS THE RELEASE\'S SEVEN YEARS ARE FOR THE WHOLE WORLD, SO THE LOAN\'S SEVEN YEARS ARE FOR THE WHOLE WORLD. ({SP_(111, 3, "שבע", "שנים", "לכל", "אחד", "ואחד")} "seven years for each one"; {SP_(111, 3, "שבע", "שנים", "לכל", "העולם")} "seven years for the whole world"): I3 (checked) — THE FIRST PARADIGM: ONE CALENDAR FOR ALL OR A PRIVATE COUNT FROM EACH LOAN — the parser\'s 15:1 [7] the number at issue; the land\'s sabbath the father. Fresh.')
srow(111, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'OR GO THIS WAY: SEVEN YEARS ARE LAID ON THE HEBREW SLAVE AND SEVEN YEARS ON THE LOAN — AS THE SLAVE\'S SEVEN YEARS ARE FOR EACH ONE, SO THE LOAN\'S SEVEN YEARS FOR EACH ONE! The row without a citation ({SP_(111, 4, "או", "כלך", "לדרך", "זו")} "or go this way"; {SP_(111, 4, "בעבד", "עברי")} "on the Hebrew slave"): THE RIVAL PARADIGM — the slave\'s years counted from his own sale (15:12; Exodus 21:2, the twin law), a private count; the English\'s note the Mekhilta\'s twin argument (neziqin 1). Fresh.')
srow(111, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'LET US SEE WHICH IT RESEMBLES: WE REASON A THING NOT DEPENDENT ON THE JUBILEE FROM A THING NOT DEPENDENT ON THE JUBILEE, AND LET NOT THE HEBREW SLAVE, WHO DEPENDS ON THE JUBILEE, PROVE. ({SP_(111, 5, "נראה", "למי", "דומה")} "let us see which it resembles"; {SP_(111, 5, "שתלוי", "ביובל")} "who depends on the jubilee"): THE TWO PARADIGMS WEIGHED BY A THIRD FEATURE — the slave goes out at the jubilee (Leviticus 25:40, the kin\'s ledger), the debt does not (112:2): the land\'s release the closer kin. Fresh.')
srow(111, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'OR GO THIS WAY: WE REASON A THING PRACTICED IN THE LAND AND OUTSIDE THE LAND FROM A THING PRACTICED IN THE LAND AND OUTSIDE THE LAND, AND LET NOT THE RELEASE OF THE SOIL, PRACTICED ONLY IN THE LAND, PROVE! The row without a citation ({SP_(111, 6, "בארץ", "ובחוצה", "לארץ")} "in the Land and outside the Land"; {SP_(111, 6, "השמט", "קרקע")} "the release of the soil"): THE COUNTER-FEATURE — the debt\'s release runs outside the Land (111:11), the soil\'s does not: each paradigm disqualified by one feature, the reasoning deadlocked (the English\'s note Sifra Behar 2:4). Fresh.')
srow(111, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'THE TEACHING SAYS "SEVEN YEARS", "SEVEN YEARS" FOR AN ANALOGY: AS THE SEVEN YEARS SAID OF THE RELEASE ARE FOR THE WHOLE WORLD, SO THE SEVEN YEARS SAID OF THE LOAN ARE FOR THE WHOLE WORLD. ({SP_(111, 7, "שבע", "שנים", "שבע", "שנים", "לגזרה", "שוה")} "seven years, seven years, for an analogy"): I2 (checked) NAMED IN THE HEBREW ITSELF — the deadlock of 111:3-6 broken by the repeated words (the English reads the second seat as 15:9\'s "the seventh year"): THE ONE CALENDAR — the release-year the world\'s, never the debtor\'s; the compile\'s parameter for the release effect (the running world\'s sabbatical count the measurement owed at 13b). Fresh.')
srow(111, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'R. YOSE THE GALILEAN SAYS: IT SAYS "THE SEVENTH YEAR, THE YEAR OF RELEASE, DRAWS NEAR" (15:9) — IF SEVEN YEARS FOR EACH ONE, HOW DOES IT DRAW NEAR? SAY THEN: SEVEN YEARS FOR THE WHOLE WORLD! ({SP_(111, 8, "היאך", "היא", "קרובה")} "how does it draw near"; {SP_(111, 8, "אמור", "מעתה")} "say then"): THE ARGUMENT FROM THE CHAPTER\'S OWN VERB — a year that "draws near" is a date every man sees coming, a public calendar; 117:4 repeats it at its verse; the parser\'s ordinal 15:9 [7]. Fresh.')
srow(111, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT THE RELEASE OF THE LOAN HAVE BEEN PRACTICED IN THE WILDERNESS? THE TEACHING SAYS "YOU SHALL MAKE A RELEASE … RELEASE" (15:1-2). ({SP_(111, 9, "נוהג", "במדבר")} "practiced in the wilderness"): THE LAW\'S ONSET ASKED — before the entry; the answer the same clause as 111:2 (the English\'s bracket "even before entering"), and 41:3 lists the release among the commandments that begin AFTER the conquest (the outside row): two readings of the onset the compile records side by side. Fresh.')
srow(111, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'OR DOES IT SAY "YOU SHALL MAKE A RELEASE … RELEASE" ONLY OF THE LAND OF ISRAEL — WHERE YOU MAKE A RELEASE FOR THE SOIL YOU RELEASE THE LOAN, AND OUTSIDE THE LAND, WHERE YOU MAKE NO RELEASE FOR THE SOIL, YOU DO NOT RELEASE THE LOAN? ({SP_(111, 10, "אלא", "בארץ", "ישראל")} "only of the Land of Israel"; {SP_(111, 10, "אין", "את", "משמט", "מלוה")} "you do not release the loan"): the counter-reading — 111:2\'s binding turned into a limit of place. Fresh.')
srow(111, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'THE TEACHING SAYS "FOR A RELEASE HAS BEEN PROCLAIMED TO THE LORD" (15:2) — BOTH IN THE LAND AND OUTSIDE THE LAND. ({SP_(111, 11, "בין", "בארץ", "ובין", "בחוצה", "לארץ")} "both in the Land and outside the Land"): THE DEBT\'S RELEASE A LAW OF THE PERSON, NOT OF THE SOIL — from the clause "to the LORD" (Onkelos "before the LORD"); 112:11 says it again at its verse; the compile: the release\'s territory EVERYWHERE where the soil\'s is THE LAND — two parameters (the English\'s note Tosefta Kiddushin 1:12). Fresh.')
srow(112, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THIS IS THE MANNER OF THE RELEASE" (15:2) — FROM HERE THEY SAID (MISHNAH SHEVIIT 10:8): ONE WHO REPAYS A DEBT IN THE SEVENTH YEAR — [THE CREDITOR] SAYS TO HIM "I RELEASE IT"; IF HE SAID "EVEN SO", HE MAY ACCEPT IT FROM HIM, BECAUSE IT IS SAID "AND THIS IS THE MANNER OF THE RELEASE". The head row of piska 112, THE MISHNAH CITED IN THE HEBREW ITSELF ({SP_(112, 1, "המחזיר", "חוב", "בשביעית")} "one who repays a debt in the seventh year"; {SP_(112, 1, "משמט", "אני")} "I release it"): THE ANSWER SHEET INSIDE THE SPINE — "the manner" (דבר "word") read as THE WORD THE CREDITOR MUST SAY, an oral declaration and no more (the English\'s note); the repayment lawful after it; routed to 13b\'s docket (Mishnah Sheviit 10:8; Gittin 37b). Fresh.')
srow(112, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'["AND THIS IS THE MANNER OF THE RELEASE"] — THE RELEASE RELEASES A LOAN, AND THE JUBILEE DOES NOT RELEASE A LOAN. The row without a citation ({SP_(112, 2, "שמטה", "משמטת", "מלוה")} "the release releases a loan"; {SP_(112, 2, "ואין", "יובל", "משמט", "מלוה")} "and the jubilee does not release a loan"): THE TWO YEARS\' POWERS DIVIDED — the seventh year\'s the debt, the fiftieth\'s the slave and the soil (Leviticus 25:10-13, the kin\'s ledger); "this" the limiting word. Fresh.')
srow(112, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'FOR IT WOULD HAVE BEEN A REASONING: IF THE RELEASE, WHICH DOES NOT FREE SLAVES, RELEASES A LOAN, THE JUBILEE, WHICH FREES SLAVES — IS IT NOT LOGICAL THAT IT RELEASE A LOAN? THE TEACHING SAYS "AND THIS IS THE MANNER OF THE RELEASE" — THE RELEASE RELEASES A LOAN AND THE JUBILEE DOES NOT. ({SP_(112, 3, "שהיה", "בדין")} "for it would have been a reasoning"; {SP_(112, 3, "אינו", "דין", "שישמט", "מלוה")} "is it not logical that it release a loan"): I1 (checked) FROM THE SEVENTH YEAR TO THE JUBILEE, BLOCKED BY THE VERSE — "this" and no other year. Fresh.')
srow(112, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'AN A FORTIORI FOR THE RELEASE TO FREE SLAVES: IF THE JUBILEE, WHICH DOES NOT RELEASE A LOAN, FREES SLAVES, THE SEVENTH YEAR, WHICH RELEASES A LOAN — IS IT NOT LOGICAL THAT IT FREE SLAVES? THE TEACHING SAYS "IN THIS YEAR OF JUBILEE" (LEVITICUS 25:13) — THE SEVENTH YEAR RELEASES A LOAN AND THE JUBILEE FREES SLAVES. ({SP_(112, 4, "קל", "וחומר", "לשמטה", "שתוציא", "עבדים")} "an a fortiori for the release to free slaves"): I1 (checked) THE REVERSE, BLOCKED BY LEVITICUS 25:13\'s "THIS" — two a fortiori arguments cancelled by two verses\' "this", each year held to its own power (the English\'s note Sifra Behar 3:6); the compile: the release effect NEVER frees a slave — 15:12\'s six years his own count (111:4\'s feature). Fresh.')
srow(112, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"EVERY CREDITOR SHALL RELEASE" — MIGHT IT BE EVEN A THEFT AND A DEPOSIT? THE TEACHING SAYS "THE LOAN OF HIS HAND". ({SP_(112, 5, "אף", "בגזלה", "ובפקדון")} "even a theft and a deposit"): THE RELEASE\'S OBJECT NARROWED TO LOANS — stolen goods and deposits not released; "the loan of his hand" the creditor\'s own word (the store\'s gloss "debt", the patch at the tail). Fresh.')
srow(112, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'OR "THE LOAN OF HIS HAND" — MIGHT IT BE A HIRELING\'S WAGE AND THE SHOP\'S CREDIT? THE TEACHING SAYS "WHICH HE LENDS TO HIS NEIGHBOR". ({SP_(112, 6, "שכר", "שכיר", "והקפת", "החנות")} "a hireling\'s wage and the shop\'s credit"): THE SECOND NARROWING — wages and store credit not loans by their words (Mishnah Sheviit 10:1 the exam\'s row: the shop\'s credit not released). Fresh.')
srow(112, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'IF IN THE END WE INCLUDE THEM ALL, WHY DOES THE TEACHING SAY "THE LOAN OF HIS HAND"? AS THE LOAN OF HIS HAND IS A STANDING DEBT, SO ALL OF THEM STANDING DEBTS. ({SP_(112, 7, "אם", "סופנו", "לרבות", "כלם")} "if in the end we include them all"; {SP_(112, 7, "בזקוף", "אף", "כלם", "זקופים")} "a standing debt, so all of them standing"): THE EXCLUSIONS REVERSED BY THE ANSWER SHEET — Mishnah Sheviit 10:1 releases the wage and the shop\'s credit once "made a loan" (the English\'s note): THE PARTICULAR TEACHES THE CLASS\'S FEATURE (I8\'s shape — named without a code): whatever is written up as a standing debt is released. Fresh.')
srow(112, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE SHALL NOT EXACT" — TO PUT HIM UNDER A PROHIBITION. ({SP_(112, 8, "לתן", "עליו", "בלא", "תעשה")} "to put him under a prohibition"): THE DUNNING CREDITOR\'S NEGATIVE COMMAND — the release an effect on the debt, the exaction a transgression of the creditor: two lines for the compile. Fresh.')
srow(112, 9, 'CONTEXT', f'"HIS NEIGHBOR" — TO THE EXCLUSION OF OTHERS. ({SP_(112, 9, "פרט", "לאחרים")} "to the exclusion of others"): the foreigner outside the bar — 15:3\'s "you may exact". Fresh.')
srow(112, 10, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND HIS BROTHER" — TO THE EXCLUSION OF THE RESIDENT ALIEN. ({SP_(112, 10, "פרט", "לגר", "תושב")} "to the exclusion of the resident alien"): the sojourner not "brother" here (14:21\'s carcass-eater the kin, read at chapter 14). Fresh.')
srow(112, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR A RELEASE HAS BEEN PROCLAIMED TO THE LORD" — BOTH IN THE LAND AND OUTSIDE THE LAND. ({SP_(112, 11, "בין", "בארץ", "בין", "בחוצה", "לארץ")} "both in the Land and outside the Land"): 111:11\'s rule at its own verse — THE TERRITORY PARAMETER said twice in the spine. Fresh.')
srow(113, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE FOREIGNER YOU MAY EXACT" (15:3) — THIS IS A POSITIVE COMMAND. The head row of piska 113 ({SP_(113, 1, "זו", "מצות", "עשה")} "this is a positive command"): THE PERMISSION READ AS A DUTY — the foreigner\'s debt exacted (Onkelos "a son of the nations", the rendering at the noun\'s four seats in the book, asserted); the compile: the foreigner\'s loan outside the release effect. Fresh.')
srow(113, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND WHAT IS YOURS WITH YOUR BROTHER" — AND NOT WHAT IS YOUR BROTHER\'S IN YOUR HAND; FROM HERE YOU SAY (MISHNAH SHEVIIT 10:2): ONE WHO LENDS ON A PLEDGE DOES NOT RELEASE. ({SP_(113, 2, "ולא", "של", "אחיך", "בידך")} "and not what is your brother\'s in your hand"; {SP_(113, 2, "המלוה", "על", "המשכון")} "one who lends on a pledge"): THE PLEDGE-LOAN OUTSIDE THE RELEASE — the creditor already holds; the Mishnah cited in the Hebrew (the English\'s note Tosefta Sheviit 8:5); 24:10-13\'s pledge law waits for its sitting. Fresh.')
srow(113, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOUR HAND SHALL RELEASE" — AND NOT ONE WHO HANDS HIS BONDS TO THE COURT. FROM HERE THEY SAID (MISHNAH SHEVIIT 10:3-4): HILLEL ORDAINED THE PROZBUL FOR THE ORDER OF THE WORLD, WHEN HE SAW THAT THE PEOPLE REFRAINED FROM LENDING ONE ANOTHER AND TRANSGRESSED WHAT IS WRITTEN IN THE TORAH; AND THIS IS THE BODY OF THE PROZBUL: "I HAND OVER TO YOU, JUDGES SO-AND-SO IN PLACE SO-AND-SO, EVERY DEBT I HAVE, THAT I MAY COLLECT IT WHENEVER I WISH" — AND THE JUDGES SIGN BELOW, OR THE WITNESSES. ({SP_(113, 3, "ולא", "המוסר", "שטרותיו", "לבית", "דין")} "and not one who hands his bonds to the court"; {SP_(113, 3, "התקין", "הלל", "פרוסבול")} "Hillel ordained the prozbul"): THE PROZBUL\'S TEXT INSIDE THE SPINE — "your hand" the limit, the court\'s hand not yours; THE CHAPTER\'S OWN WARNING (15:9) THE ORDINANCE\'S REASON — the law\'s foreseen failure repaired by a procedure the verse leaves open; the exam: Mishnah Sheviit 10:3-4, Mishnah Gittin 4:3, Gittin 36a-37a (routed to 13b\'s docket). Fresh.')
srow(114, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"HOWBEIT THERE SHALL BE NO NEEDY AMONG YOU" (15:4), AND THERE IT SAYS "FOR THE NEEDY SHALL NEVER CEASE FROM THE MIDST OF THE LAND" (15:11)! WHEN YOU DO THE WILL OF THE PLACE — THE NEEDY ARE AMONG OTHERS; AND WHEN YOU DO NOT DO THE WILL OF THE PLACE — THE NEEDY ARE AMONG YOU. The head row of piska 114 ({SP_(114, 1, "אביונים", "באחרים")} "the needy among others"; {SP_(114, 1, "אביונים", "בכם")} "the needy among you"): THE CHAPTER\'S TWO VERSES SET AGAINST EACH OTHER (asserted: three tokens shared in order) AND RECONCILED BY A CONDITION, NOT A THIRD VERSE (I13\'s question without its third verse — no code claimed): "among you" the conditional\'s variable — the compile: 15:4 the blessing\'s arm, 15:11 the default state; 118:1 the same reading at the other verse. Fresh.')
srow(114, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR THE LORD WILL SURELY BLESS YOU IN THE LAND" — IT TELLS THAT THE BLESSING DEPENDS ONLY ON THE LAND. ({SP_(114, 2, "שאין", "ברכה", "תלויה", "אלא", "בארץ")} "the blessing depends only on the Land"): THE BLESSING\'S PLACE — "bless, He will bless you" ONE seat in this form (asserted; Abraham\'s "bless, I will bless you" the form\'s first); 11:13-17\'s rain the kin, read at chapter 11. Fresh.')
srow(114, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'"WHICH THE LORD YOUR GOD GIVES YOU FOR AN INHERITANCE TO POSSESS" — AS A REWARD FOR POSSESSING, YOU WILL CONQUER. ({SP_(114, 3, "בשכר", "שתירש", "תכבש")} "as a reward for possessing you will conquer"): the formula\'s clause read as cause and reward (25:19\'s twin ahead, asserted). Fresh.')
srow(115, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"ONLY IF YOU DILIGENTLY HEARKEN TO THE VOICE OF THE LORD YOUR GOD" (15:5) — FROM HERE THEY SAID: IF A MAN HEARD A LITTLE, THEY LET HIM HEAR MUCH; IF A MAN HEARD WORDS OF TORAH, THEY LET HIM HEAR WORDS OF THE SCRIBES. The head row of piska 115 ({SP_(115, 1, "שמע", "אדם", "קמעה")} "if a man heard a little"; {SP_(115, 1, "דברי", "תורה")} "words of Torah"; {SP_(115, 1, "דברי", "סופרים")} "words of the scribes"): THE DOUBLED VERB (the infinitive absolute "hear, you shall hear", the chapter\'s third of eight) READ AS A HEARING THAT GROWS — AND THE ORAL LAW NAMED AS THE SECOND HEARING, the words of the scribes after the written Torah: the code/data law\'s own seat in the spine; 11:13\'s "hearken, you shall hearken" the twin (asserted: Onkelos\'s "receive, you shall receive the Memra" at 11:13, 15:5, 28:1). Fresh.')
srow(115, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO KEEP TO DO ALL THIS COMMANDMENT" — THAT A LIGHT COMMANDMENT BE AS DEAR TO YOU AS A WEIGHTY COMMANDMENT. ({SP_(115, 2, "מצוה", "קלה", "חביבה", "עליך", "כמצוה", "חמורה")} "a light commandment as dear to you as a weighty commandment"): "ALL THIS COMMANDMENT" READ AS EVERY COMMANDMENT WEIGHED ALIKE (the English\'s note Mishnah Avot 2:1; piska 79:1\'s twin at 11:22); the singular "commandment" the chapter\'s register. Fresh.')
srow(116, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR THE LORD YOUR GOD HAS BLESSED YOU AS HE SPOKE TO YOU" (15:6) — AND WHAT DID HE SPEAK TO YOU? "BLESSED SHALL YOU BE IN THE CITY …" (28:3). The head row of piska 116 ({SP_(116, 1, "ומה", "דבר", "לך")} "and what did He speak to you"; {SP_(116, 1, "ברוך", "אתה", "בעיר")} "blessed shall you be in the city"): THE RECEIPT\'S SHAPE WITHOUT THE NAME (asserted: "as He spoke to you" four in the book; the finder finds no receipt) GIVEN ITS REFERENT BY THE SHELF — A VERSE AHEAD, 28:3, the blessing chapter\'s first line: THE POINTER RUNS FORWARD, to a promise the book has not yet spoken, not back to an act on the tape (11:25\'s receipt pointed back to Exodus 23:27 by two teachers) — for the compile a labeled HYPOTHESIS until 28:3 is read at its sitting; NEVER READ AHEAD; the English\'s note the Mekhilta\'s parallel (pischa 12). Fresh.')
srow(116, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL LEND TO MANY NATIONS" — MIGHT YOU BORROW AT A SELA AND LEND AT A SHEKEL, AS OTHERS DO? THE TEACHING SAYS "AND YOU SHALL NOT BORROW". ({SP_(116, 2, "לווה", "בסלע", "ומלוה", "בשקל")} "borrow at a sela and lend at a shekel"): THE TWO CLAUSES READ TOGETHER — the lending not a trade on the margin, the money-changer\'s way (the English\'s "as do the others"); 28:12\'s twin "you shall lend to many nations and not borrow" waits for its sitting (asserted the twin with the other verb). Fresh.')
srow(116, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL RULE OVER MANY NATIONS" — MIGHT YOU RULE OTHERS AND OTHERS RULE YOU, AS IT IS SAID "AND ADONI-BEZEK SAID: SEVENTY KINGS …" (JUDGES 1:7)? THEREFORE IT IS SAID "AND THEY SHALL NOT RULE OVER YOU". ({SP_(116, 3, "מושל", "באחרים", "ואחרים", "מושלים", "בך")} "rule others and others rule you"): THE RUN\'S CASE FROM JUDGES — the king who fed seventy kings under his table repaid in kind; the verse\'s second clause bars the wheel\'s turn. Fresh.')
srow(116, 4, 'CONTEXT', f'"IF THERE BE AMONG YOU" (15:7) — AND NOT AMONG OTHERS. ({SP_(116, 4, "ולא", "באחרים")} "and not among others"): the poor of Israel the law\'s subject (the exam: Bava Metzia 71a\'s order). Fresh.')
srow(116, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"A NEEDY ONE" — THE HUNGRIER FIRST. ({SP_(116, 5, "תאב", "תאב", "קודם")} "the hungrier first"): THE WORD READ BY ITS ROOT (the needy the one who craves — the English\'s "hungriest of the hungry") — the first of the row-set\'s PRECEDENCE RULES (116:5-8): a ranking the compile carries as a parameter (the exam: Bava Metzia 71a). Fresh.')
srow(116, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOUR BROTHER" — THIS IS YOUR BROTHER BY YOUR FATHER; WHEN IT SAYS "OF ONE OF YOUR BROTHERS" — IT TEACHES THAT YOUR BROTHER BY YOUR FATHER PRECEDES YOUR BROTHER BY YOUR MOTHER. ({SP_(116, 6, "אחיך", "מאביך", "קודם", "לאחיך", "מאמך")} "your brother by your father precedes your brother by your mother"): THE SECOND RANK — the paternal line first, the inheritance\'s line (Numbers 27\'s daughters the kin, read at THE TENT). Fresh.')
srow(116, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"IN ONE OF YOUR GATES" — THE DWELLERS OF YOUR CITY PRECEDE THE DWELLERS OF ANOTHER CITY. ({SP_(116, 7, "יושבי", "עירך", "קודמים")} "the dwellers of your city precede"): THE THIRD RANK — the formula "within one of your gates" at its first seat of four (asserted: 16:5, 17:2, 23:17 ahead) read as the town\'s own poor first (the exam: Bava Metzia 71a, "the poor of your city"). Fresh.')
srow(116, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"IN YOUR LAND" — THE DWELLERS OF THE LAND PRECEDE THE DWELLERS OUTSIDE THE LAND. WHEN IT SAYS "IN ONE OF YOUR GATES": IF HE DWELT IN ONE PLACE YOU ARE COMMANDED TO SUPPORT HIM; IF HE WENT ROUND THE DOORS, YOU ARE NOT BOUND TO HIM FOR ANYTHING. ({SP_(116, 8, "יושבי", "הארץ", "קודמים")} "the dwellers of the Land precede"; {SP_(116, 8, "מחזר", "על", "הפתחים")} "went round the doors"): THE FOURTH RANK AND THE BEGGAR\'S CASE — the settled poor supported from the town, the door-to-door beggar owed nothing from its fund (the English reads it as a question; the note Tosefta Peah 4:8); the beggar\'s seat in the exam (Bava Batra 9a) outside 13b\'s listed shelf — noted for the union rule. Fresh.')
srow(116, 9, 'CONTEXT', f'"WHICH THE LORD YOUR GOD GIVES YOU" — IN EVERY PLACE. ({SP_(116, 9, "בכל", "מקום")} "in every place"): the duty everywhere, the ranks inside it. Fresh.')
srow(116, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT HARDEN YOUR HEART" (15:7) — THERE IS A MAN WHO AGONIZES WHETHER TO GIVE OR NOT TO GIVE. ({SP_(116, 10, "שמצטער", "אם", "יתן", "אם", "לא", "יתן")} "who agonizes whether to give or not to give"): THE HEART\'S CLAUSE A STATE BEFORE THE HAND\'S — "harden" the verb of Sihon\'s heart (2:30, the book\'s other seat, asserted). Fresh.')
srow(116, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL NOT SHUT YOUR HAND" — THERE IS A MAN WHO STRETCHES OUT HIS HAND AND DRAWS IT BACK AND SHUTS IT. ({SP_(116, 11, "שפושט", "את", "ידו", "וחוזר", "וקופצה")} "who stretches out his hand and draws it back and shuts it"): THE HAND\'S CLAUSE THE SECOND STATE — "shut" the verb\'s one seat in the Torah (asserted; Onkelos keeps the root). Fresh.')
srow(116, 12, 'MATERIAL', f'"FROM YOUR NEEDY BROTHER" — IF YOU DO NOT GIVE HIM, IN THE END YOU WILL TAKE FROM HIM. WHENCE THAT IF YOU OPENED ONCE YOU OPEN EVEN A HUNDRED TIMES? THE TEACHING SAYS "FOR OPEN, YOU SHALL OPEN YOUR HAND TO HIM" (15:8). ({SP_(116, 12, "סופך", "לטול", "הימנו")} "in the end you will take from him"; {SP_(116, 12, "אפלו", "מאה", "פעמים")} "even a hundred times"): THE WHEEL AND THE DOUBLING — the giver\'s own future need the first reason; the infinitive absolute "open, you shall open" (the chapter\'s fourth of eight) read as REPEAT WITHOUT LIMIT (117:6 the same from "give, you shall give"; Bava Metzia 31b the exam\'s seat for the doublings). Fresh.')
srow(116, 13, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND LEND, YOU SHALL LEND HIM" — "OPEN, YOU SHALL OPEN": OPEN TO HIM WITH WORDS; IF HE IS ASHAMED, SAY TO HIM "YOU NEED A LOAN". FROM HERE THEY SAID: CHARITY IS GIVEN AS A LOAN. ({SP_(116, 13, "פתח", "לו", "בדברים")} "open to him with words"; {SP_(116, 13, "צדקה", "נתנת", "כמלוה")} "charity is given as a loan"): THE GIFT DRESSED AS A LOAN FOR THE ASHAMED — the mouth opened before the hand (the English\'s note Tosefta Peah 4:12; one editor reads the passage as an interpolation). Fresh.')
srow(116, 14, 'MATERIAL', f'"LEND, YOU SHALL LEND HIM" — THEY GIVE HIM AND THEN TAKE A PLEDGE FROM HIM: R. JUDAH\'S WORDS. AND THE SAGES SAY: THEY TELL HIM "BRING A PLEDGE", TO SET HIS MIND AT EASE. ({SP_(116, 14, "דברי", "רבי", "יהודה")} "R. Judah\'s words"; {SP_(116, 14, "וחכמים", "אומרים")} "and the sages say"; {SP_(116, 14, "להגיס", "את", "דעתו")} "to set his mind at ease"): A DISPUTE ON THE PLEDGE — the gift then the pledge (R. Judah) or the pledge asked to spare his pride (the sages): a two-arm parameter for the compile (the English\'s note Tosefta Peah 4:12; the exam: Ketubot 67b). Fresh.')
srow(116, 15, 'MATERIAL', f'"SUFFICIENT FOR HIS NEED" — YOU ARE NOT COMMANDED TO MAKE HIM RICH. ({SP_(116, 15, "אין", "אתה", "מצוה", "לעשרו")} "you are not commanded to make him rich"): THE UPPER BOUND — "need" the Torah\'s one seat of the noun (asserted); the exam: Mishnah Peah 8:7, Ketubot 67b. Fresh.')
srow(116, 16, 'MATERIAL', f'"THAT WHICH HE LACKS" — EVEN A HORSE, EVEN A SLAVE. ({SP_(116, 16, "אפלו", "סוס", "ואפלו", "עבד")} "even a horse, even a slave"): THE BOUND MEASURED BY THE MAN — his former standard, not the town\'s (Ketubot 67b the exam\'s seat). Fresh.')
srow(116, 17, 'MATERIAL', f'A DEED OF HILLEL THE ELDER, WHO GAVE A POOR MAN OF GOOD FAMILY A HORSE TO EXERCISE ON AND A SLAVE TO SERVE HIM; AND AGAIN A DEED IN UPPER GALILEE, WHERE THEY BROUGHT A GUEST A LITRA OF MEAT EVERY DAY. The row without a citation ({SP_(116, 17, "מעשה", "בהלל", "הזקן")} "a deed of Hillel the Elder"; {SP_(116, 17, "ליטרא", "בשר", "בכל", "יום")} "a litra of meat every day"): TWO DEEDS AS THE MEASURE\'S PROOF — narrative rows inside a law piska (the English\'s note Tosefta Peah 4:10; Ketubot 67b tells Hillel running before the horse himself). Fresh.')
srow(116, 18, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR HIM" — THIS IS A WIFE, AS IT IS SAID "I WILL MAKE FOR HIM A HELPER" (GENESIS 2:18). ({SP_(116, 18, "לו", "זו", "אשה")} "for him — this is a wife"; {SP_(116, 18, "אעשה", "לו", "עזר")} "I will make for him a helper"): THE PRONOUN\'S REACH — the wife inside "his need" by the "for him" of Genesis 2:18 (the English\'s note Tosefta Ketubot 6:8; Ketubot 67b: they even marry him a wife). REREAD WHOLE (the Genesis 2 sitting, gen_09_helper_woman_first_speech).')
